        "original_id": "aca7e76e-9acd-5175-bfaa-c8261a85d107",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2012 United States Libertarian National Convention\n- Organizations: Libertarian Party, Republican Party\n- People: Gary Johnson\n- Places: Las Vegas, Nevada; Red Rock Resort Spa and Casino; New Mexico\n- Roles: President of the United States, Vice President of the United States, Governor of New Mexico\n\nFacts:\n- Gary Johnson was born on January 1, 1953.\n- Gary Johnson is an American businessman, author, and politician.\n- Gary Johnson served as the 29th Governor of New Mexico from 1995 to 2003 as a member of the Republican Party.\n- The 2012 United States Libertarian National Convention was held from May 2 to May 6, 2012 in Las Vegas, Nevada at the Red Rock Resort Spa and Casino.\n- Delegates of the Libertarian Party used the 2012 United States Libertarian National Convention to choose the party's nominees for President of the United States and Vice President of the United States in the 2012 general election.\n- Gary Johnson, a former Governor of New Mexico, won the Libertarian presidential nomination on the first ballot at the 2012 United States Libertarian National Convention.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "07303615-5980-55e3-a9b0-8f70e3d9c2b8",
